# Estimate AI Testing Rule (2026-10-28)

Read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/AI_HANDOFF.md`, `docs/DOMAIN_RULES.md` and the
relevant tests before making changes. Run `python -m pytest -q` on the
user-provided project ZIP **before and after** every meaningful change,
including a documentation-only release.

For bug fixes, first reproduce the failure with a test; then fix the root
cause with the smallest safe change. Business-rule changes require realistic
positive and negative tests, ideally anonymized from real workbooks.

Do not weaken validation to make tests pass. Never invent prices or silently
change historical VBA-derived behavior; keep RNMC live matching separate
from TKP winner imports and experimental TKP shadow comparisons.

The reference baseline for the supplied ZIP on 2026-10-28 was 362 passed,
1 skipped. It is not an invariant or a substitute for rerunning tests.
Always report exact test totals and files changed, and deliver a ZIP, not
a patch. For database work also check PRAGMA integrity_check and
foreign_key_check on isolated copies.
